  "content": {
    "id": "p14-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Evaluate\n$$\\frac1{\\sqrt4+\\sqrt6}+\\frac1{\\sqrt6+\\sqrt8}+\\cdots+\\frac1{\\sqrt{98}+\\sqrt{100}}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$4$\n\nRationalise each term; cancellation leaves $\\dfrac{\\sqrt{100}-\\sqrt4}{2}$.",
      "worked": "For each term,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac1{\\sqrt n+\\sqrt{n+2}}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{n+2}-\\sqrt n}{(n+2)-n}\\\\\\frac1{\\sqrt n+\\sqrt{n+2}}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{n+2}-\\sqrt n}{2}.\\end{align*}$$\nWriting the required sum as $S$,\n$$\\begin{align*}S&=\\frac12\\big[(\\sqrt6-\\sqrt4)+(\\sqrt8-\\sqrt6)+\\cdots+(\\sqrt{100}-\\sqrt{98})\\big]\\\\S&=\\frac{\\sqrt{100}-\\sqrt4}{2}\\\\S&=\\frac{10-2}{2}\\\\S&=4.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 72
  },
